    "/api/v1/tools/meta_list_custom_audiences/execute": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "meta_list_custom_audiences",
        "summary": "List Meta custom and lookalike audiences",
        "description": "Lists the saved custom and lookalike audiences on the ad account with their type, approximate size and whether Meta considers them usable right now.\nUse when: planning retargeting or exclusions, or when the user refers to an audience by name and you need its id.\nDo not assume an audience is usable because it exists — Meta refuses to deliver to audiences below roughly a thousand people, and the delivery status says so.\nReturns each audience id plus its subtype (website, customer list, engagement, lookalike), which decides whether it makes sense as a target or only as an exclusion.\nIf an audience is too small, say so and suggest broadening rather than launching against it.",
