        "description": "Stops delivery on one ad group without touching the rest of the campaign. Spend on it drops to zero; nothing is deleted, the ads underneath keep their configuration and review history, and chatgpt_resume_ad_group starts it again.\nUse when: the user wants to stop one part of a campaign — a test that is not working, an audience that is too expensive — and you have shown them what it is currently spending.\nDo not pause on one or two days of data: this platform's daily numbers are noisy at small budgets. Show last_7_days from chatgpt_get_performance at ad_group level first.\nDo not use this as a way to delete. Pausing is reversible; archiving is not.\nReturns the ad group read back from the platform, which is how the pause is confirmed rather than assumed.",
