    "/api/v1/tools/chatgpt_pause_campaign/execute": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "chatgpt_pause_campaign",
        "summary": "Pause a ChatGPT Ads campaign",
        "description": "Stops delivery on one campaign by setting it to paused. Spend stops; nothing is deleted, every ad group and ad underneath keeps its configuration and history, and the campaign can be started again with chatgpt_resume_campaign.\nUse when: the user has explicitly asked to stop something, and you have shown them what it is currently spending.\nDo not pause on the strength of a day or two of data — this platform's daily numbers are noisy at small budgets. Show the user last_7_days from chatgpt_get_performance and let them decide.\nDo not use this as a way to delete. Pausing is reversible; archiving is not, and no tool here archives anything.\nReturns the campaign read back from the platform, which is how you confirm the pause actually applied rather than reporting an intention as a fact.",
