    "/api/v1/tools/chatgpt_resume_ad_group/execute": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "chatgpt_resume_ad_group",
        "summary": "Resume a ChatGPT Ads ad group",
        "description": "Sets one ad group back to active so it can deliver again. Real money is spent as soon as the platform approves delivery.\nUse when: the user has reviewed something paused — often an ad group this server created — and wants it live.\nDo not resume without telling the user what it bids and what the campaign's spend limits are: the campaign budget is shared with every other ad group under it.\nDo not assume \"active\" means \"delivering\". An ad group inside a paused campaign still delivers nothing, and an unapproved ad delivers nothing either — check the read-back and chatgpt_list_ads.\nReturns the ad group read back from the platform with its bidding configuration and any serving issue.",
