    "/api/v1/tools/chatgpt_resume_campaign/execute": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "chatgpt_resume_campaign",
        "summary": "Resume a ChatGPT Ads campaign",
        "description": "Sets one campaign back to active so it can deliver again. Real money starts being spent as soon as the platform approves delivery.\nUse when: the user has reviewed something paused — often a campaign this server created — and wants it live.\nDo not resume without telling the user the spend limits first: resuming restarts the whole structure underneath, and the daily limit applies from that moment.\nDo not assume \"active\" means \"delivering\". Check the read-back: an unapproved account, an unapproved ad or a serving issue will keep an active campaign at zero, and the serving issues in the read-back say which.\nReturns the campaign read back from the platform, including its spend limits and any serving issue.",
